From: Fabio Fantoni <fabio.fantoni@m2r.biz>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:20:30 +0100
Subject: [winpr,sysinfo] fix NEON detection on Linux aarch64

IsProcessorFeaturePresent(PF_ARM_NEON_INSTRUCTIONS_AVAILABLE) tests
getauxval(AT_HWCAP) against HWCAP_NEON (1 << 12), which is the 32 bit
ARM layout from arch/arm/include/uapi/asm/hwcap.h. On aarch64 the kernel
reports Advanced SIMD as HWCAP_ASIMD (1 << 1), and bit 12 is
HWCAP_ASIMDRDM (arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/hwcap.h).

So on CPUs without the ARMv8.1 RDM extension, like the Cortex-A72 of the
Raspberry Pi 4 (AT_HWCAP 0x887: fp asimd evtstrm crc32 cpuid), every
NEON primitive and codec is disabled and the generic C code is used. On
a Cortex-A76 (Raspberry Pi 5) NEON is enabled only because RDM happens
to be present.

Since #11998 the NEON sources are built for aarch64, so this runtime
check now decides whether they are used.

Check HWCAP_ASIMD on aarch64 and keep HWCAP_NEON for 32 bit ARM.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Forwarded: no
---
 winpr/libwinpr/sysinfo/sysinfo.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/winpr/libwinpr/sysinfo/sysinfo.c b/winpr/libwinpr/sysinfo/sysinfo.c
index 966fe16..55c10cb 100644
--- a/winpr/libwinpr/sysinfo/sysinfo.c
+++ b/winpr/libwinpr/sysinfo/sysinfo.c
@@ -1153,6 +1153,9 @@ static void cpuid(unsigned info, unsigned* eax, unsigned* ebx, unsigned* ecx, un
 #define HWCAP_VFPD32 (1 << 19) /* set if VFP has 32 regs (not 16) */
 #define HWCAP_IDIV (HWCAP_IDIVA | HWCAP_IDIVT)
 
+// AArch64 uses a different layout - arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/hwcap.h
+#define ARM64_HWCAP_ASIMD (1 << 1)
+
 // From linux kernel uapi/linux/auxvec.h
 #define AT_HWCAP 16
 
@@ -1260,8 +1263,11 @@ BOOL IsProcessorFeaturePresent(DWORD ProcessorFeature)
 	{
 		case PF_ARM_NEON_INSTRUCTIONS_AVAILABLE:
 		case PF_ARM_NEON:
-
+#if defined(_M_ARM64)
+			if (caps & ARM64_HWCAP_ASIMD)
+#else
 			if (caps & HWCAP_NEON)
+#endif
 				ret = TRUE;
 
 			break;
